# BENEFITS D2.2 — Microsimulation. Single root ignore.
# NO MICRODATA IN THIS TREE. Real FRS (PolicyEngine) and EU-SILC (EUROMOD)
# microdata are licensed and live OUTSIDE this repo, in the sibling ../LOCAL_ONLY.
# This file is the backstop for any microdata a later local run regenerates in-tree.

# ── Microdata and tabular data formats (regenerated locally; never committed) ──
*.parquet
*.csv
*.dta
*.sav

# ── Keep the synthetic CI fixture and the aggregate WEVM tables (data-free) ──
!uk/model/demo/per_unit_export.parquet
!uk/docs/wevm_deciles_2023_24.csv
!uk/docs/wevm_headline_2023_24.csv
!uk/docs/wevm_takeup_sensitivity_eps1.csv

# ── Licensed raw survey inputs and intermediates (belt-and-braces) ─────────
**/FRS_data/**
**/UDB_*
**/inputs/**
**/processed/**

# ── Engine binaries and non-redistributed software ────────────────────────
**/EM_Executable*
*.dll

# ── Retired artefacts, kept on disk and out of the repository ─────────────
# Superseded tools and workbooks are moved here rather than deleted. This rule
# lived only in .git/info/exclude, which is local to one clone and does not
# travel: a fresh clone would have started tracking every retired file. Moved
# here on 2026-08-01 so the rule is part of the repository it protects.
_superseded/

# ── Engine run logs (regenerated on every run; the evidence copy lives in docs) ──
europe/logs/

# ── Suite counts, written by check_browser.py on a clean four-tool run ────────
# Read by the export stamper from the working tree so the published README cannot
# misstate how many assertions ran. A per-run measurement, not evidence: regenerate
# it by running the suite rather than carrying it.
.suite_counts.json

# ── Environments and caches ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ── Operating-system cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# ── Generated audit table (audit_provider_params.py output) ──────────────
PROVIDER_PARAM_AUDIT.md
